beb1a44c-0fcb-49d7-a0de-f2b9fad8d699	King West	king-west	\N	Toronto's densest club strip. King Street West between Bathurst and Spadina is the epicentre of bottle service, high-energy dance floors, and late-night lineups.	43.6441	-79.4023	1
383a41fb-2083-43aa-a068-26d45757bc85	Entertainment District	entertainment-district	\N	Home to the city's biggest venues — Rebel, Coda, Toybox. Best for EDM, large-capacity shows, and sporting-event overflow.	43.6474	-79.387	2
6df9f72e-1789-412a-a0da-de9d9593de36	Kensington Market	kensington-market	\N	Eclectic, indie, anti-mainstream. Dive bars, patio hangs, reggae and world music. The anti-King-West.	43.654	-79.4009	3
29e01fa7-721e-4ff4-9c41-021747751c1f	Little Italy	little-italy	\N	College Street's laid-back Italian corridor. Sidewalk patios, aperitivo culture, and a creative local crowd. Great for a slow evening that turns into a late one.	43.6553	-79.4196	5
3207c69e-becb-4206-a455-d5ee8b37c68f	Ossington	ossington	\N	Toronto's cocktail corridor. Low-key, creative-crowd bars. Best for first dates and pre-drinks.	43.6522	-79.4243	4
5ae9e8f9-1a23-4e15-8cca-f2e107686ddc	Leslieville	leslieville	\N	East-end chill. Neighbourhood bars, live music, patio culture. More locals than tourists.	43.661	-79.3313	8
4803d631-9311-43ec-8c42-e7367300663e	Church-Wellesley Village	church-wellesley	\N	The heart of Toronto's LGBTQ+ scene. Inclusive, high-energy, welcoming to all.	43.6651	-79.381	6
2a34c935-caeb-4468-8829-61ba46d190e3	Distillery District	distillery-district	\N	Cobblestone streets, upscale cocktail bars, artisanal everything. Date-night central.	43.6503	-79.3595	7
7f5dba86-dffb-49fc-8194-fc2ad50a4ba4	Annex	annex	\N	Student-meets-intellectual on Bloor Street West. Cozy pubs, indie concert venues, and late-night spots that stay real no matter how trendy the rest of the city gets.	43.67	-79.4085	9
d9680c1f-c788-4bcf-8b9f-c3ca668600c4	Yorkville	yorkville	\N	Toronto's upscale playground. Rooftop lounges, bottle-service hotspots, and cocktail bars dressed in designer lighting. For when you want to look the part.	43.6718	-79.3924	10
5895b548-404c-430d-b831-ec5c3c245bd9	Scarborough	scarborough	\N	The east end's underrated nightlife belt. Diverse food-and-drink scene, Caribbean and South Asian influences, and a local community energy you won't find downtown.	43.7735	-79.2577	12
49c4b4e3-c539-4b66-b641-eb61181ce198	North York	north-york	\N	Yonge and Sheppard's dense mixed-use corridor anchors North York's nights — karaoke rooms, izakayas, and K-pop lounges alongside mainstream bars and clubs.	43.7615	-79.4111	11
